// dcdsp_acoustic_irs.h — GENERATED acoustic body impulse responses. Do not
// hand-edit.
//
// Three synthetic guitar-body IRs, minimum-phase, authored at 48 kHz,
// 2048 taps (42.7 ms). Recipe (offline generator, cepstral min-phase
// reconstruction of an authored magnitude target): Helmholtz air resonance
// (~100-120 Hz, Q 11-13, +6.5-9.5 dB), top/back plate modes (~190-320 Hz),
// mid character shaping, string-body reflection combs (1-5.5 ms,
// a = 0.20-0.35) and gentle HF shading. Levels normalized to 0 dB log-mean
// over 500-2000 Hz, so blending against a unit delta only adds the body
// coloration. Minimum-phase => zero reported latency.
//
// Body order: 0 = parlor, 1 = OM, 2 = dreadnought (the `body` knob morphs
// small->large while raising the blend).
